# .env.example — copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local `npm run dev`/
# `npm run preview`. Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars into the CLIENT
# bundle at BUILD time — different mechanism from .dev.vars (Wrangler's
# server-side runtime secrets, see .dev.vars.example), and different
# again from production, where this needs to be set as a build-time
# environment variable in Cloudflare Workers Builds' own dashboard
# config, not committed here either way.

# Cloudflare's own published Turnstile TESTING sitekey — "always passes
# with visible widget," documented at
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
# Paired with the TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY test value in .dev.vars.example.
# For production, replace with a real sitekey from a Turnstile widget
# registered in the Cloudflare dashboard against this site's real domain
# — never this test value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
